# Production Environment Secrets Template
#
# This file documents the required secrets for the production environment.
# Add these secrets to GitHub: Settings → Environments → production → Environment secrets
#
# DO NOT commit actual secret values to this file!
# SECURITY WARNING: Production secrets must be highly secure and rotated regularly!

# ============================================================================
# Database Configuration
# ============================================================================

# PostgreSQL connection string for production database
# Format: postgresql://username:password@host:port/database
# Example: postgresql://push_user:secure_pass@prod-db.example.com:5432/push_platform
# IMPORTANT: Use strong passwords and restrict IP access to database
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/database

# ============================================================================
# Firebase Configuration (Production)
# ============================================================================

# Firebase service account JSON for production
# This is required for production to use service account authentication
# Get from Firebase Console → Project Settings → Service Accounts → Generate new private key
# Format: Single-line escaped JSON string
# Example: {"type":"service_account","project_id":"my-project","private_key_id":"...","private_key":"-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n","client_email":"...","client_id":"...","auth_uri":"...","token_uri":"...","auth_provider_x509_cert_url":"...","client_x509_cert_url":"..."}
SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON={"type":"service_account","project_id":"..."}

# ============================================================================
# API Security
# ============================================================================

# Comma-separated list of valid API keys for production
# Generate cryptographically secure random keys (minimum 64 characters recommended)
# Use: openssl rand -hex 32
# Example: a1b2c3d4e5f6...,f6e5d4c3b2a1...
# IMPORTANT: Rotate these keys every 90 days
API_KEYS=production-key-1,production-key-2,production-key-3

# ============================================================================
# Deployment URLs (Optional but Recommended)
# ============================================================================

# Production API URL for health checks and deployment tracking
# Example: https://api.example.com
# If not set, health checks will be skipped
API_URL=https://api.example.com

# Production Worker URL for deployment tracking
# Example: https://worker.example.com
# Used for deployment status updates
WORKER_URL=https://worker.example.com

# ============================================================================
# Platform-Specific Secrets (Optional)
# ============================================================================

# Only add these if you're using the specific platform for deployment

# Railway
# Get from Railway Dashboard → Settings → Tokens
# Create a production-specific token with limited permissions
# RAILWAY_TOKEN=your-railway-token

# Google Cloud Run
# Service account JSON key (download from GCP Console)
# Use a dedicated service account with minimal required permissions
# GCP_SA_KEY={"type":"service_account","project_id":"..."}
# GCP_PROJECT_ID=your-gcp-project-id

# AWS ECS/Fargate
# Get from AWS IAM → Users → Security credentials
# Use a dedicated IAM user with minimal required permissions
# Enable MFA for production AWS access
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your-aws-access-key
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your-aws-secret-key

# Generic Docker Host (SSH)
# SSH credentials for deployment
# Use SSH key authentication (not password)
# Restrict SSH key to specific commands if possible
# SERVER_HOST=production.example.com
# SERVER_USER=deploy
# SSH_PRIVATE_KEY=-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----...

# ============================================================================
# Security Best Practices
# ============================================================================
#
# 1. Use unique, strong secrets for production (never reuse staging secrets)
# 2. Generate cryptographically secure random values:
#    - API Keys: openssl rand -hex 32 (64 characters)
#    - Database passwords: 32+ characters, mix of upper/lower/numbers/symbols
# 3. Rotate secrets regularly:
#    - API Keys: Every 90 days
#    - Database passwords: Every 180 days
#    - Service account keys: Annually
# 4. Limit access:
#    - Only authorized team members should have access to production secrets
#    - Use GitHub environment protection rules with required reviewers
#    - Enable audit logging for secret access
# 5. Monitor:
#    - Set up alerts for unauthorized access attempts
#    - Monitor API key usage patterns
#    - Log all deployment activities
# 6. Backup:
#    - Store encrypted backup of secrets in secure location (e.g., 1Password, Vault)
#    - Document secret rotation procedures
#    - Maintain emergency access procedures
#
# ============================================================================
# Environment Protection Rules
# ============================================================================
#
# For production environment, configure these protection rules in GitHub:
#
# 1. Required reviewers:
#    - Add at least 2 team members who must approve deployments
#    - Ensure reviewers have different roles (e.g., dev + ops)
#
# 2. Wait timer:
#    - Optional: Set 5-10 minute wait before deployment starts
#    - Allows time to review and cancel if needed
#
# 3. Deployment branches:
#    - Restrict to tags matching pattern: v*.*.*
#    - Prevents accidental deployment from feature branches
#
# 4. Environment secrets:
#    - Use environment-level secrets (not repository-level)
#    - Ensures isolation between staging and production
#
# ============================================================================
# Instructions
# ============================================================================
#
# 1. Copy this template to use as reference (store securely, not in repo)
# 2. Generate actual secret values using secure methods:
#    - API Keys: openssl rand -hex 32
#    - Passwords: Password manager with 32+ character setting
#    - Service accounts: Download from provider console
# 3. Add secrets to GitHub:
#    - Go to repository Settings
#    - Click Environments
#    - Select "production"
#    - Configure protection rules (required reviewers, etc.)
#    - Click "Add secret"
#    - Enter secret name and value
#    - Click "Add secret"
# 4. Verify secrets are set before running production deployment
# 5. Document secret values in your organization's secret management system
# 6. Set up secret rotation reminders (90 days for API keys)
#
# For detailed instructions, see: .github/DEPLOYMENT.md
#
# ============================================================================
# Compliance and Audit
# ============================================================================
#
# If your organization has compliance requirements (SOC2, HIPAA, etc.):
#
# 1. Document who has access to production secrets
# 2. Maintain audit log of secret changes and rotations
# 3. Implement automated secret scanning in CI/CD
# 4. Use secret management service (HashiCorp Vault, AWS Secrets Manager, etc.)
# 5. Ensure secrets are encrypted at rest and in transit
# 6. Regular security audits of deployment processes
#
